module gunbc.rung_drop.consumed_row_owner_charge_unenforced

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, DeletedWithoutReplacement }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }

// DECLARED 2026-09-16 beside the change that lowers the rung (gunbc#11481), which removed the two
// merge_group follow-up arms of wave_admission_refusal on an operator ruling that mandating a
// deletion follow-up pull request is not worth its cost.
//
// BOTH REMOVALS ARE DROPS AND EACH HAS ITS OWN ROW. An earlier revision of this row said only one
// was, on the ground that OwnerFollowUpAbsent established a number had been TYPED and nothing more.
// That is true of its GREEN and does not make it a decoration -- section 4b reserves that word for a
// check whose forbidden state cannot be expressed anywhere the check could run, and that arm's RED
// was authorable and fired. Review 67014 caught it. The owner-side class is declared separately at
// gunbc.rung_drop.owner_deletion_follow_up_charge_removed, which is where the reasoning lives.
//
// THIS ROW IS FOR ConsumedRowOwnerChargeBypassed, whose lost coverage is a different class with a
// different restoration trigger: its RED discriminated on the ABSENCE of any number on a BYSTANDER
// composition, and what has to come back is the ability to adjudicate a consumed row at all.
//
// WHY THE LANDING ARM DOES NOT COVER IT, measured rather than assumed. The surviving consumed-row
// arm fires when roster_due, and roster_due is base == head OR roster_touched. Lane ruling
// (fierce-lark-661, 2026-09-13) moved the required verdict off the push to the default branch, and
// with it the only run where base == head. On the required path roster_due is therefore
// roster_touched alone, so a base-consumed row whose owner authored no follow-up now refuses on no
// required run until somebody happens to edit the roster directory. An earlier revision of the
// gunbc#11481 change claimed otherwise; that claim was wrong and review 66992 caught it.

data consumed_row_owner_charge_unenforced: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "consumed_row_owner_charge_unenforced" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "a transition-admission row consumed at the base, whose owning change authored no deletion_follow_up, is refused on some required run before the roster is next touched",

  declared: "2026-09-16",

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: DeletedWithoutReplacement,
    population: [
      "base-consumed transition-admission rows whose owning change authored no deletion_follow_up, on any merge_group composition that does not touch dag/gunbc/namespace/transition_admission/"
    ],
    restoration_trigger: "UN-RETIRED 2026-09-20, AND THE CLASS IS NOW SUBSUMED. This row was retired on 2026-09-19 by gunbc#11704, whose carrier made a tree-resident admission refuse at its owner's own gate on every required run. gunbc#11774 then DELETED the namespace-wave-admission wall outright on an operator ruling, and with it the carrier, the roster and the phase -- so the capability that fired this trigger no longer exists and the retirement is un-done rather than left standing on a mechanism the tree does not carry (DESIGN section 4b(1): the reported rung must equal the rung established by executed evidence). WHAT IS TRUE NOW: the subject of this row -- a consumed transition-admission row refused on some required run -- has no constructor at all, because there is no roster and no wall. That is not this row's trigger firing; it is the whole class moving inside gunbc.rung_drop.namespace_wave_admission_wall_removed, which declares the wall's loss and carries the restoration trigger for it. Read that row, not this one, for what is uncovered today. This row is kept as the record of the 2026-09-16 removal and its 2026-09-19 repair, and it is retired only by its own trigger below. FORMER trigger_fired: 2026-09-19 -- THE CAPABILITY, IN ITS STRONGER FORM, AND NO ARM RE-ADDED. Transition admissions are carried by the change that needs them (a transition_admission block in its commit messages, read base..head by v1_compiler.namespace_wave_admission load_carried_admissions) and never by the tree, and tree_carried_admission_refusal refuses ANY file under dag/gunbc/namespace/transition_admission/ on EVERY required run -- the pull_request run and the merge_group run of the composition that actually lands -- with no dependence on base == head or on the roster being touched. A row that could become base-consumed therefore refuses at its OWNER's own gate, before it lands, and a base-consumed row on main has no constructor. Nobody is charged: no follow-up is mandated and no bystander composition is billed, so neither of the removed arms returns. EXECUTED EVIDENCE, LOCAL NOT ENROLLED (a Rust test target no CI step runs -- gunbc.rung_drop.rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path; executed on BuildBuddy 2026-09-19; the enrolled mechanism is the gate on the required namespace-wave-admission phase): wave_admission_carrier a_row_file_in_the_tree_refuses_at_its_owners_own_gate drives run_wave_admission_between over a real repository through three changes over one base -- the bare move refuses as unadjudicated (control), the move with a tree row refuses naming the row and the remedy (RED), the move with the carried block is admitted by that row and lands a tree holding no admission (positive control). RESTORED RUNG: 2, mechanically preventable, the declared previous rung -- now on every required run rather than on a roster touch, and on the change that caused the row rather than after it landed. NOT HIGHER: a row file is still writable and is kept off main by the required gate executing. Population at retirement: the one row standing on main (gunbc#11660's enrollment_id_for_code binding) is deleted by the same change.

THE CAPABILITY: a required run that adjudicates a consumed transition-admission row WITHOUT depending on base == head or on the roster being touched -- that is, the consumed-row charge evaluated on the composition that actually lands, the way the merge queue now supplies the required verdict. Nothing smaller retires this row. In particular, re-adding a merge_group arm that refuses a BYSTANDER composition does not: that was the arm removed here, it billed a change for a debt its own comment said was not its own, and DESIGN section 5 names that externalization. Nor does authoring follow-up numbers on the rows standing today, which changes the population and not the coverage. The debt itself stays visible meanwhile: used_without_follow_up is still counted in the refusal message, and deletion_follow_up is still carried on every row.",
  }
}
